(2269695, 307079, 21197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by KingWampum:</b></div><hr/><i> FACT 1)  Justin read the thread where a member of the site council states that a photo should "LOOK LIKE TWO SECONDS" as opposed to being two seconds.  This is no fault of Justin. THIS IS A VERY IMPORTANT POINT THAT IS CONVENIENTLY OVERLOOKED AGAIN AND AGAIN.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Fact - details of challenges are noted in the challenge itself. <br/>Fact - challenge details quote, "Take a photograph using a shutter speed of exactly 2 seconds."<br/>Fact - it''s a nice photograph <br/>Fact - it doesn''t comply with the challenge<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by KingWampum: FACT 1)  Justin read the thread where a member of the site council states that a photo should "LOOK LIKE TWO SECONDS" as opposed to being two seconds.  This is no fault of Justin. THIS IS A VERY IMPORTANT POINT THAT IS CONVENIENTLY OVERLOOKED AGAIN AND AGAIN.  Fact - details of challenges are noted in the challenge itself. Fact - challenge details quote, "Take a photograph using a shutter speed of exactly 2 seconds."Fact - it''s a nice photograph Fact - it doesn''t comply with the challenge', '2006-03-29 11:48:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2270070, 308871, 32321, '<td valign="top">Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>First Impression:<br/>Nice shot! I like the way the lines lead my eyes to the black hole<br/> <br/>Composition:<br/>Really like the crop and the angle of your shot. B&amp;W really works at highlighting the lines/curves. <br/> <br/>Subject:<br/>Given the forum traffic for this challenge, you met the challenge! (Thank you for a 2 second exposure!)<br/> <br/>Technical:<br/>I actually disagree with some of the comments below. I find the picture a bit grainy and the focus a little soft. Maybe its a monitor calibration issue. You mentioned sharpening twice. If you USM after resizing, you can make the picture a little more crisp.<br/> <br/>Summary:<br/>What were the chances of me drawing your picture again? I like the shot and your perspective. As mentioned below, the notion of time was not conveyed in you picture.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi! Heres a comment from the Critique Club. First Impression:Nice shot! I like the way the lines lead my eyes to the black hole Composition:Really like the crop and the angle of your shot. B&W really works at highlighting the lines/curves.  Subject:Given the forum traffic for this challenge, you met the challenge! (Thank you for a 2 second exposure!) Technical:I actually disagree with some of the comments below. I find the picture a bit grainy and the focus a little soft. Maybe its a monitor calibration issue. You mentioned sharpening twice. If you USM after resizing, you can make the picture a little more crisp. Summary:What were the chances of me drawing your picture again? I like the shot and your perspective. As mentioned below, the notion of time was not conveyed in you picture. ', '2006-03-29 13:26:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2270094, 307079, 33515, '<td valign="top">Justin, the bottom line is you presented a wonderful photo that has the look and feel of the challenge description. Well done and congrats on the blue!</td>', 'Justin, the bottom line is you presented a wonderful photo that has the look and feel of the challenge description. Well done and congrats on the blue!', '2006-03-29 13:33:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2270501, 307019, 18450, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot!!</td>', 'Beautiful shot!!', '2006-03-29 15:26:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2270535, 308526, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>Hi woutje :)<br/> <br/>This is an excellent photo and I believe the voters agreed.  Graphicfunk''s post challenge comment sums up why this photo is appealing.  It has simple visual appeal and it does meet the challenge very well.  It''s clean and simple.  Photos that show a great execution of a technique (like long exposures) generally do well.  I can''t offer you any suggestions for improvement on this because I don''t think there are any.  Excellent work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... Hi woutje :) This is an excellent photo and I believe the voters agreed.  Graphicfunk''s post challenge comment sums up why this photo is appealing.  It has simple visual appeal and it does meet the challenge very well.  It''s clean and simple.  Photos that show a great execution of a technique (like long exposures) generally do well.  I can''t offer you any suggestions for improvement on this because I don''t think there are any.  Excellent work :) John Setzler', '2006-03-29 15:34:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2270625, 308871, 8891, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the critique, Bruce!</td>', 'Thanks for the critique, Bruce!', '2006-03-29 15:55:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2270844, 308383, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Rushing Rapids" is a great addition into the water challenge.  I was really happy to see so many different perspectives.<br/> <br/>The image itself is very intriguing, I think the colors you captured separated it from the other water entries.  The glow from the water is a very amazing blue.  I like the composition of the shot, the branches and rocks make a nice framing that is nice placed and not forced.   The lighting in the shot looks nice, it can be a challenge to use the natural light, but you did a great job. Great timing to capture the movement of the water.<br/> <br/>You defiantly have a great grasp on the the challenge, only your second challenge and still doing amazing.  Keep up the good work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Rushing Rapids" is a great addition into the water challenge.  I was really happy to see so many different perspectives. The image itself is very intriguing, I think the colors you captured separated it from the other water entries.  The glow from the water is a very amazing blue.  I like the composition of the shot, the branches and rocks make a nice framing that is nice placed and not forced.   The lighting in the shot looks nice, it can be a challenge to use the natural light, but you did a great job. Great timing to capture the movement of the water. You defiantly have a great grasp on the the challenge, only your second challenge and still doing amazing.  Keep up the good work.', '2006-03-29 16:44:27.000000', NULL, 0),
