(2272309, 307151, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Ominous Sky" is a nice addition into the 2- Second challenge.  It was nice to see a different idea and concept for the challenge.  <br/> <br/>The image itself grabs the viewers attention, it has to with such an enormous sky.  I would have the same opinion as many of the voters have listed, this is an excellent shot but the garage takes away from the score.  I think the lighting on the garage just grabs your eye an takes you away from the sky.  The lighting on the house itself is great and is very different from the usual.  The lighting overall is just interesting, did you happen to have a car parked out there with the headlights on? The angle from the shadows cast by the trees would make think so.  The composition is nice, I love how you were able to capture the sky.  This was a great shot and I think you had a wonderful idea.  I can''t wait to see your future challenges.  <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "Ominous Sky" is a nice addition into the 2- Second challenge.  It was nice to see a different idea and concept for the challenge.   The image itself grabs the viewers attention, it has to with such an enormous sky.  I would have the same opinion as many of the voters have listed, this is an excellent shot but the garage takes away from the score.  I think the lighting on the garage just grabs your eye an takes you away from the sky.  The lighting on the house itself is great and is very different from the usual.  The lighting overall is just interesting, did you happen to have a car parked out there with the headlights on? The angle from the shadows cast by the trees would make think so.  The composition is nice, I love how you were able to capture the sky.  This was a great shot and I think you had a wonderful idea.  I can''t wait to see your future challenges.  ', '2006-03-30 02:24:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2272327, 307740, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"In 2 seconds sir" is a piece that definatly grabs your attention in the 2 second challenge.  You have defiantly meet the qualifications of the challenge.  <br/> <br/>I love how bold you were with the piece.  The color choice was probably a love it or hate it factor for voters.  I personally love the contrast.  I would be curious to see a white background but I really think compared to this one it would just seem dull.  It is amazing how much the liquid looks unreal, almost like a ribbon, especially in the stream.  I really am surprised you didn''t score higher.  Most the time bright, full frame images just capture the voters.  <br/> <br/>I think you composition is just prefect, not too tight at all.  Too much more of the glass would take away from the movement of the liquid.  Really great work here.</td>', '*Critique Club* "In 2 seconds sir" is a piece that definatly grabs your attention in the 2 second challenge.  You have defiantly meet the qualifications of the challenge.   I love how bold you were with the piece.  The color choice was probably a love it or hate it factor for voters.  I personally love the contrast.  I would be curious to see a white background but I really think compared to this one it would just seem dull.  It is amazing how much the liquid looks unreal, almost like a ribbon, especially in the stream.  I really am surprised you didn''t score higher.  Most the time bright, full frame images just capture the voters.   I think you composition is just prefect, not too tight at all.  Too much more of the glass would take away from the movement of the liquid.  Really great work here.', '2006-03-30 02:33:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2272346, 308423, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"HARD ROCK, SOFT WATER" does meet the qualification of the 2 second challenge.  I think you had a great idea in trying to capture a close up of the water and its movement.  <br/> <br/>Looking at the image, it seems over exposed.  The colors are a little too bright, especially on the leaves the almost look unreal. The timing of the water was nice.  I think the shot is framed very well.  You left the leaves in the shot, which allows you to stand out from the rest of the water/waterfall entries.  Also the focus seems a little off, possibly the camera was not on a sturdy tripos while you had the 2 seconds going. <br/> <br/>Unfortunately I really think the exposer hurt this piece.  But I was looking at your portfolio and based on your work, I really have to wonder if you wanted the shot to look like this.  Even more so since you named the piece HARD ROCK maybe you were trying to go with an edgy/harsh piece.</td>', '*Critique Club* "HARD ROCK, SOFT WATER" does meet the qualification of the 2 second challenge.  I think you had a great idea in trying to capture a close up of the water and its movement.   Looking at the image, it seems over exposed.  The colors are a little too bright, especially on the leaves the almost look unreal. The timing of the water was nice.  I think the shot is framed very well.  You left the leaves in the shot, which allows you to stand out from the rest of the water/waterfall entries.  Also the focus seems a little off, possibly the camera was not on a sturdy tripos while you had the 2 seconds going.  Unfortunately I really think the exposer hurt this piece.  But I was looking at your portfolio and based on your work, I really have to wonder if you wanted the shot to look like this.  Even more so since you named the piece HARD ROCK maybe you were trying to go with an edgy/harsh piece.', '2006-03-30 02:42:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2272353, 308245, 42013, '<td valign="top">A perfect set of three waterfalls. Personally, i like the touch of warmth in the reflection at the top of the falls to contrast with the cold blue of the ice and water.  Great finish.<br/> <br/>Now if you just had a pug in an inflatable kayak...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-03-30 01:47:03.</i></td>', 'A perfect set of three waterfalls. Personally, i like the touch of warmth in the reflection at the top of the falls to contrast with the cold blue of the ice and water.  Great finish. Now if you just had a pug in an inflatable kayak...', '2006-03-30 02:46:37.000000', '2006-03-30 02:47:03.000000', 0),
(2272374, 307896, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"2 Seconds Call'' is a great addition into the 2 second challenge.  Originally ideas are always great to see.  This one looks like out of the box idea, which usually is a big hit with the voters.<br/> <br/>The image is very interesting and I think you had an excellent idea.  I love that you were able to cut off each end and not have a drag from the light to the outside edges of the frame, that would have ruined the shot for me.  I am surprised that it your shot didn''t score higher, maybe because we just recently had the Painting with light challenge.  The cropping of the shot feels just right, and I am glad you were able to produce a solid black backdrop with the piece.  Personally I think you did a good job and I hope to see future entries from you!</td>', '*Critique Club* "2 Seconds Call'' is a great addition into the 2 second challenge.  Originally ideas are always great to see.  This one looks like out of the box idea, which usually is a big hit with the voters. The image is very interesting and I think you had an excellent idea.  I love that you were able to cut off each end and not have a drag from the light to the outside edges of the frame, that would have ruined the shot for me.  I am surprised that it your shot didn''t score higher, maybe because we just recently had the Painting with light challenge.  The cropping of the shot feels just right, and I am glad you were able to produce a solid black backdrop with the piece.  Personally I think you did a good job and I hope to see future entries from you!', '2006-03-30 02:53:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2272490, 307591, 17148, '<td valign="top">:: Critique Club ::<br/> <br/>As far as meeting the challengeyou did. As far as making an interesting or appealing photo I would say it is lacking. The only focus here is the camera which is the subject only to show that it is a 2-sec exposurewhich it really doesnt do that either because that camera isnt taking the picture. If you had something in the photo that made you look to the background and tie your image together I think it would have been better. Maybe if you had set the camera up all the way to the right with a small streak of the cars going by. I think you tried hard to think outside the box and shoot something original and I give you points for that. Next time look at the whole photo as one and see what else can hold the viewers attention. <br/></td>', ':: Critique Club :: As far as meeting the challengeyou did. As far as making an interesting or appealing photo I would say it is lacking. The only focus here is the camera which is the subject only to show that it is a 2-sec exposurewhich it really doesnt do that either because that camera isnt taking the picture. If you had something in the photo that made you look to the background and tie your image together I think it would have been better. Maybe if you had set the camera up all the way to the right with a small streak of the cars going by. I think you tried hard to think outside the box and shoot something original and I give you points for that. Next time look at the whole photo as one and see what else can hold the viewers attention. ', '2006-03-30 04:23:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2272499, 306689, 17148, '<td valign="top">:: Critique Club ::<br/> <br/>I dont care that it is your filler imageit looks very cool. I have seen shots like this before but I think this is the only one with other cars in the photo alsoI like it very muchthe colors, the lights, the motionit all works here. I know this is all about the setupthe end image is more of luck and how many shots you take to make sure you got something good. Well your setup was perfect and from that you got a wonderful image. <br/></td>', ':: Critique Club :: I dont care that it is your filler imageit looks very cool. I have seen shots like this before but I think this is the only one with other cars in the photo alsoI like it very muchthe colors, the lights, the motionit all works here. I know this is all about the setupthe end image is more of luck and how many shots you take to make sure you got something good. Well your setup was perfect and from that you got a wonderful image. ', '2006-03-30 04:28:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2272505, 308119, 17148, '<td valign="top">:: Critique Club ::<br/> <br/>Very odd feel to this. I like how strange and original it is thoughcan see it took a bit of brain power to make it happen. Nitpicking I would have not cut the top of the photo so close to the handgiven it a little more room. Thinking your choice of blue to symbolize coldness or even lifelessness has a certain weight to the imageother just might think it looks too weird. I think you did a great job shooting for the challenge and being creative at the same time. <br/></td>', ':: Critique Club :: Very odd feel to this. I like how strange and original it is thoughcan see it took a bit of brain power to make it happen. Nitpicking I would have not cut the top of the photo so close to the handgiven it a little more room. Thinking your choice of blue to symbolize coldness or even lifelessness has a certain weight to the imageother just might think it looks too weird. I think you did a great job shooting for the challenge and being creative at the same time. ', '2006-03-30 04:33:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2273657, 307196, 39057, '<td valign="top">Edit: After seeing other shots the are in the top 20 of many of the challenges that DNMC I feel that as long as the Advanced or Basic rules are not broken, there is no need for DQ or Self DQ.<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-30 23:06:14.</i></td>', 'Edit: After seeing other shots the are in the top 20 of many of the challenges that DNMC I feel that as long as the Advanced or Basic rules are not broken, there is no need for DQ or Self DQ. ', '2006-03-30 15:13:52.000000', '2006-05-31 00:06:14.000000', 0),
